{"name":"Necrophilic Brown","hex":"#dead69","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"necrophilic","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of or relating to necrophilia."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/necrophilic"},{"term":"brown","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour like that of chocolate or coffee.","One of the colour balls used in snooker, with a value of 4 points."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a brown color/colour.","Gloomy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brown"}],"entries":[{"title":"Necrophilia","blocks":[{"text":"Necrophilia, also known as necrophilism, necrolagnia, necrocoitus, necrochlesis, and thanatophilia, is sexual attraction or acts involving corpses, including both direct intercourse with corpses and sexual excitement at the thought or presence of one. It is classified as a paraphilia by the World Health Organization (WHO) in its International Classification of Diseases (ICD) diagnostic manual, as well as by the American Psychiatric Association in its Diagnostic and Statistical Manual (DSM). Reported motivations vary widely, ranging between sexual domination of a non-responsive partner, fetishization of death and corpses, and bereavement of a close sexual partner. Necrophilia can coincide with sexual roleplay of the subject instead pretending to be a corpse while their partner takes on the role of the necrophile."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Pietro_Pajetta_-_Der_Hass_-_1896.jpg/330px-Pietro_Pajetta_-_Der_Hass_-_1896.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Necrophilia","wikidata":"Q181843"},{"title":"Brown","blocks":[{"text":"Brown is a color. It can be thought as a darker, typically desaturated shade of orange, and can often be produced by combining red and yellow with another color, namely blue."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Espresso-roasted_coffee_beans.jpg/330px-Espresso-roasted_coffee_beans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brown","wikidata":"Q47071"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Pierre_Zaccone%2C_Histoire_des_bagnes%2C_depuis_leur_cr%C3%A9ation_jusqu%27%C3%A0_nos_jours_-_Le_Vampire.jpg/500px-Pierre_Zaccone%2C_Histoire_des_bagnes%2C_depuis_leur_cr%C3%A9ation_jusqu%27%C3%A0_nos_jours_-_Le_Vampire.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Pierre_Zaccone%2C_Histoire_des_bagnes%2C_depuis_leur_cr%C3%A9ation_jusqu%27%C3%A0_nos_jours_-_Le_Vampire.jpg/1280px-Pierre_Zaccone%2C_Histoire_des_bagnes%2C_depuis_leur_cr%C3%A9ation_jusqu%27%C3%A0_nos_jours_-_Le_Vampire.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Pierre_Zaccone%2C_Histoire_des_bagnes%2C_depuis_leur_cr%C3%A9ation_jusqu%27%C3%A0_nos_jours_-_Le_Vampire.jpg/500px-Pierre_Zaccone%2C_Histoire_des_bagnes%2C_depuis_leur_cr%C3%A9ation_jusqu%27%C3%A0_nos_jours_-_Le_Vampire.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Vampire, engraving depicting Sergeant François Bertrand, 1878","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APierre_Zaccone%2C_Histoire_des_bagnes%2C_depuis_leur_cr%C3%A9ation_jusqu'%C3%A0_nos_jours_-_Le_Vampire.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Salvator_merianae_-_necrophilia.jpg/500px-Salvator_merianae_-_necrophilia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Salvator_merianae_-_necrophilia.jpg/500px-Salvator_merianae_-_necrophilia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A male black